From 4b6078292a2b194ab5799e2449bca0a9ebdf01ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Curling collisions: stones exchange their speed along the
 line between their centres

Two free stones that touch exchange the part of their speed that runs along the line between their centres and keep the rest, and only when they are closing in. The original shared the speed by the angle alone and moved both stones by guessed amounts: a stone hit on its side left along the thrower's line, the thrown stone stopped dead, and a grazing touch could leave the pair inside each other, colliding again in every step. The repeat of the last collision step ended only when nothing touched, so that pair hung the game; it now repeats eight times at most. Stones on a peg collide as before.
---
